WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.520
What’s good y’all? This week, we doublin’
down wit The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:27.180
Mr. Hyde, by Robert Louis Stevenson. Lawyer-man
John Utterson swangin’ down da streets of

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:33.330
London when his cous Enfield start givin him
the DL on a CRAZY-a** story. Brutha like:

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.861
“Yo- Back in da winter I peeped this shady
cat named Hyde straight STOMP a b**** JUST

00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:43.820
CUZ she bumped into him. Soon as I saw dat
mess, I told him he best throw a C-note her

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.120
way or else me and this mob gonna turn
this into a scandal.” Hyde like “Psh.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:54.020
fine” and oblige a brutha, but dat check
is signed by an uptown gangsta with solid

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.460
rep, which Enfield thinkin’ is hella strange.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.989
Soon Utterson recognize that da name on the
check is a client of his named Dr. Jekyll.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:07.859
So after grubbin at da crib, Utterson check
his files and learn dat this Jekyll cat is

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:14.579
leavin all his cheddar to Mr. Hyde. Hm. Dat
don’t sound right. Utterson decide to drop

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:20.899
in on one of Jekyll’s homeboys, Dr. Lanyon.
But Lanyon say he ain’t seein Dr. J’s

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:26.170
crazy a** since they had a beef about his
bulls*** research ten years ago. Utterson

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:31.329
start scopin’ out a spot dat Hyde been seen
at. Boy creepin up on da house one night when

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:37.829
Hyde rolls by. They conversate fo’ a sec
befo’ Hyde ducks into a lab behind Jekyll’s

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:42.569
pad. After a dinner party up at Jekyll’s,
Utterson ask him what the deal is with Mr.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:46.999
Hyde. But Dr. J just shakes that load off
and say “don’t trip bout dat, baby.”

00:01:46.999 --> 00:01:53.920
Nearly a year later, Utterson get word that
somebody in town got iced, so he pay a visit

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.200
to the po-lice. Turns out, Mr. Hyde dun ghosted
one of his old crusty clients. Utterson leads

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.900
the fuzz to Hyde’s traphouse, but dude ain’t
nowhere to be found. Utterson hit up Dr. J

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:10.280
to get some answers, but Jekyll say “I don’t
f*** with that dude no mo. He long gone.”

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:16.079
and hands him a note from Hyde sayin he’s
sorry for all his bulls***. Thang is, though,

00:02:16.079 --> 00:02:23.251
both Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde got da same handwriting.
Hmmm! Fo the next two months Doctor J back

00:02:23.251 --> 00:02:28.400
to his regular self, but dat don’t last
long. Soon he don’t let anyone come to his

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:34.280
crib no mo, and next thing you know- his bro
Dr. Lanyon drops dead. Lanyon leave Utterson

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:40.060
a letter. But he ain’t s’posed to open
it til something raw happen to Jekyll. What?!

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:45.240
S*** gets real when Jekyll’s butler tell
Utterson that Doc J dun locked his self in

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:51.060
dat lab fo MONTHS! And the voice on the other
side of the door sho as HELL ain’t Jekyll’s.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:57.099
Maybe he been merced! So the two of em’
break the door down, an’ find Mr. Hyde dead

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:02.019
in Jekyll’s clothes. From da look of it,
dude killed hisself by sippin on some poison

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:07.349
juice. Utterson find an updated will, a note
tellin him to read lanyon’s letter, and

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:13.129
a confession from Hyde that gonna explain
errything. Utterson head home to read Lanyon’s

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:18.799
letter, which say he started losin his damn
mind when he saw Mr. Hyde turn into Dr. Jekyll.

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:24.530
Da shock ate at his mind til it eventually
put him in the ground. Da second letter sayin

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.950
how Dr. J been turning himslf into a nappy
monster that bring out da dark side of his

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:35.750
personality. Dat way, he can do cray s***
on the reg without no consequences. Doc Jekyll

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:40.920
was havin a good ol time morphin into dat
gnarly beast til he started transforming in

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:46.629
his SLEEP. Knowin this s*** too cray to keep
in line, the doc kicked da habit for a while,

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:52.609
but when he startin jonezin fo dem dark deeds,
he gave in, turned in to Hyde, and merced

00:03:52.609 --> 00:03:53.609
dat old geezer.

00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:58.480
After a while, Jekyll lose so much control
dat he start morphin’ into Hyde durin’

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:04.959
the DAY. So he hit up Dr. Lanyon fo some syrup
to change him back. Sadly, Jekyll just kept

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:09.980
transformin’. Eventually brutha couldn’
find da legit goods to make the amount of

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.650
serum to keep Hyde in check. Knowin dat he
gonna be Mr. Hyde fo’eva soon, he decide

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:20.780
to off his-self. His letter end by sayin he
got a new will leavin’ Utterson all his

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.560
cheddar. So this ending ain’t ALL bad!

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.280
Any literary OG’ll tell you Jekyll an’ Hyde

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:36.300
is a primo example of gothic lit. It’s packin’
everythang you’d expect: night scenes, s****y

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:41.350
weather, viscious deaths, TRANSFO’MATIONS,
a creepy house wit scurry secrets, an’ a

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:47.390
freaky lab wit more dark corners than a porno
theater. God DAMN! But da darkest thing goin

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:52.590
down in this novella ain’t even dat- it’s
what Stevenson sayin’ bout human nature.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:57.790
See back in his day, scientists thought dat
one half of yo brain reppin a certain kinda

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:02.670
personality and desires, and da other half
reppin da exact opposite.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:07.470
Righteous balla Jekyll was smart, chill an
civilized ‘cause that’s what doctors thought

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:12.910
da left side of the brain was like. Whereas
Mr. Hyde is always comin’ out HARD gettin

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:18.420
all savage n’ s*** cuz homies thought the
right half was mo’ primal and impulsive.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:24.610
Stevenson slangin images of animals to associate
Hyde with dat beastly side. This nappy scrub

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:29.670
growls like a dog and throws his limbs around
like a damn monkey! Perhaps it ain’t even

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:34.680
dat he look like an animal, but just dat Mr.
Hyde’s soul is so evil, people just THINK

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.680
he a fiend!

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:56.940
Or maybe he s’posed to represent da OG beastie:
dat hater-snake from the Garden of Eden. When

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:01.690
he morphs back into Jekyll in front of Dr.
Lanyon, he talk in hisses, an’ even try

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:06.170
to f*** wit Lanyon’s head by appealing to
his desire for dank-a** knowledge:

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:24.770
Dat boy might as well be the devil tempting
Eve to grub on dat apple from the tree of

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:30.230
knowledge! But Lanyon ain’t the only dude
to see a lil Hell in Hyde. Jekyll talk bout

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:36.120
his other half as “that child of hell,”
and Utterson says he see “satan’s signature”

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:42.350
in Hyde’s face. Dayum! Hyde’s mug is so
janky, it’s like he’s straight up bible-level

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:47.480
evil. Da real question we all gotz to ask
ourselves is: Are we all on da same struggle

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:52.260
as po’ Dr. Jekyll? Are we all one drink
away from becoming MONSTERS?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:56.940
Maybe Stevenson’s jam is a warning
about livin’ in denial. No one can keep

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.690
their dark side hidden forever. So you should
be be true to yo’self and recognize da good

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:07.360
AND bad parts. Only then can a brutha truly
find balance. You feel me?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.040
Yo, thanks for checkin out Thug Notes. Peace
yall!

